[ ] Extend the graph fixture to recurring plans and objective states =v5-fixture-gaps $The graph fixture in specifications/examples/conformance/graph covers every action field and state, charters, objectives, contexts and waits, but not: an .ics recurring plan with a materialized occurrence (when/recurrence, RRULE text, occurrence as part of the recurring action), and an objective state, whose vocabulary objectives.md does not define yet (Decision 5 says objectives have state, confirmed by an agent). Settle the objective state values with the objectives-into-Core work, then add both to the workspace, expected.ttl and the shapes, with an invalid graph for each new rule. Decision 45: the gaps apply to both expected-app.ttl and expected.ttl. ADDED 2026-10-02: ontology.md's Application Graph leaves Recurrence unspecified (the recurring plan and its rule; occurrences are ordinary actions) and objective states undefined (app.shapes.ttl forbids app:state on objectives until they are). Settle both in app: terms first, then their CCO mapping.$ !3 ^2026-10-01T22:27 #01a0fb14-c5e6-73d8-9c0d-f56f11ce00a6
[ ] Show the actions that serve an objective =objective-actions-view $Moved out of the objectives action, 2026-10-01: answering it is a query (an objective's plans, then everything they contain), which V5 makes a has-continuant-part walk from the plans that name the objective. Write it as a saved query once v5-queries has moved the queries to the new graph, then surface it in the CLI and nvim like the other named queries.$ !3 ^2026-10-01T22:35 <01a0faa2-71a3-70a1-91c5-a485dedd4de2 #01a0fb1c-4455-7218-bc00-d4d38247de78
[ ] Lint empty windows and plans outside them in Core =window-lints $Decision 48 added E008 Empty Window and W015 Planned Outside the Window to specifications/linting.md (Decision 51: E008 also catches an @ block that ends at or before it starts, Planned::is_empty, and W015 compares the whole block), with example pairs in examples/linting/. Core does not implement either, and nothing in the gate consumes those examples, so no test is red: write the failing test first (from the example pairs), then the rules. E008 uses Due::is_empty over the effective window (own : intersected with ancestors'); W015 compares @ plus its duration against it. Also the older coherence warning (a local bound outside an ancestor's window) still has no code.$ !2 ^2026-10-02T18:37 #01a0ff69-2133-7a51-8986-501607134857
[ ] Move the application vocabulary's IRIs to clearhead.dev =migrate-iris $Decision 49. Replace https://clearhead.us/ with https://clearhead.dev/ for app: (vocab/app/v1#), the shapes (specifications/app-shapes, graph-shapes) and the examples, in specifications, the fixtures, the ontology's v5 files and Core's constants. Leave v4 IRIs alone: retire-v4 deletes them. Check: grep finds clearhead.us only in v4 files and history. NOTE 2026-10-03: do NOT change the context namespace UUID 0d8937ce-eb24-52d2-9532-39ea299f888b, even though ontology.md says it was derived from https://clearhead.us/context. The UUID is the constant; changing it would rename every context node. Reword the provenance sentence only.$ !2 ^2026-10-02T23:45 #01a10083-2595-77fb-9e1d-24d741f9cbed
